    {
      "id": "reviews_4",
      "cite": "Deuteronomy 6:6–7",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "reviews_4_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "These commandments are to be on your hearts. Impress them on your children. Talk about them when you sit at home and when you walk along the road, when you lie down and when you get up.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "moses",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "reviews_5",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "Choose life 🌱",
          "note": "Love the LORD, obey him, hold fast to him — he is your life."
        },
        {
          "label": "Drift along the old paths 🍂",
          "note": "The old paths lead back toward the gods of the nations around them. Moses has already warned what that costs."
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "reviews_5_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "He set before them blessings for obedience and warnings for turning away — and then he asked for a decision. He was speaking to a people about to cross a river he would never cross himself.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
